---
// input: user-selected local Markdown files from a folder or multi-file picker
// output: browser-only OKF bundle validation report with file, link, and resource checks
// pos: OKF folder validator route (update rule: sync this header and src/pages README when this file changes)
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const sampleBundle = `bundle/
  index.md
  llms.txt (optional public entry point; not read by this validator)
  pages/home.md
  support/contact.md`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="OKF Folder Validator: Check Bundle Links and Structure"
  description="Check an OKF folder in your browser for index coverage, duplicate resources, relative links, frontmatter gaps, and bundle structure before publishing."
  path="/okf-folder-validator/"
>
  <main class="page-shell">
    <section class="page-hero narrow-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Browser-only bundle tool</p>
      <h1>OKF Folder Validator: check a local knowledge bundle</h1>
      <p class="hero-copy">
        Check a local OKF bundle folder before publishing. The browser reads only selected Markdown files, reports folder structure findings such as duplicate resources and relative links, and does not upload your files to this website.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="validator-layout">
      <div class="validator-panel">
        <div class="tool-header">
          <h2>Choose folder or files</h2>
          <button type="button" class="button ghost small" id="load-sample-bundle">Load sample bundle</button>
        </div>
        <label class="tool-label" for="folder-input">Choose OKF folder or Markdown files</label>
        <input id="folder-input" class="file-input" type="file" multiple webkitdirectory aria-describedby="folder-input-note" />
        <p class="tool-note" id="folder-input-note">
          Chrome and Edge support folder selection. If your browser does not, select multiple `.md` or `.markdown` files instead. The page reads Markdown files only, with size limits to protect the browser.
        </p>
        <button type="button" class="button primary" id="validate-folder-button">Validate OKF bundle</button>
      </div>
      <aside class="validator-panel result-panel">
        <div class="tool-header">
          <h2>Bundle report</h2>
          <button type="button" class="button ghost small" id="copy-folder-result">Copy report</button>
        </div>
        <div id="folder-validator-status" class="status-badge">Not checked</div>
        <pre id="folder-validator-output" tabindex="0">Choose a folder or load the sample bundle.</pre>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Why folder validation matters</h2>
      <p>
        The single-file OKF validator checks one pasted Markdown document. This folder validator checks how files work together: bundle layout, `index.md`, repeated resources, and relative links between Markdown files. An optional `llms.txt` file can point readers to the bundle, but this tool does not read or validate it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="compare-table-section">
      <h2>OKF bundle validation checks</h2>
      <h3>Index files</h3>
      <p>A root <code>index.md</code> helps readers and agents inspect the bundle scope before opening every file.</p>
      <h3>Duplicate resources</h3>
      <p>Repeated <code>resource</code> values usually mean two files describe the same source and need review.</p>
      <h3>Relative links</h3>
      <p>Relative Markdown links should point to files that exist inside the selected folder.</p>
      <h3>Frontmatter consistency</h3>
      <p>Each Markdown file should expose parseable frontmatter and a clear <code>type</code> field.</p>
      <div class="compare-table" role="table" aria-label="OKF bundle validation checks">
        <div class="compare-row compare-head" role="row">
          <div role="columnheader">Problem</div>
          <div role="columnheader">Why it matters</div>
          <div role="columnheader">Fix route</div>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-row" role="row">
          <div role="cell">Markdown files</div>
          <div role="cell">A bundle should contain reviewable `.md` concept files.</div>
          <div role="cell">Select `.md` or `.markdown` files.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-row" role="row">
          <div role="cell">Simple frontmatter</div>
          <div role="cell">Machines need predictable metadata before reading the body.</div>
          <div role="cell"><a href="/okf-validator/">Fix one file first</a>.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-row" role="row">
          <div role="cell">type field</div>
          <div role="cell">The draft OKF field checked by this guide must identify the concept kind.</div>
          <div role="cell"><a href="/guides/common-okf-validation-errors/">Review common errors</a>.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-row" role="row">
          <div role="cell">index.md</div>
          <div role="cell">A root index helps humans and agents inspect the bundle before opening every file.</div>
          <div role="cell">Add a root <code>index.md</code>.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-row" role="row">
          <div role="cell">Internal links</div>
          <div role="cell">Relative Markdown links should point to files that exist inside the selected bundle.</div>
          <div role="cell">Fix paths or add the target file.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-row" role="row">
          <div role="cell">Duplicate resource</div>
          <div role="cell">Repeated canonical resources usually mean two files describe the same concept.</div>
          <div role="cell">Merge overlap or split concepts clearly.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Repair order</h2>
      <ol class="step-list">
        <li>Select an OKF folder or several Markdown files.</li>
        <li>The page filters for Markdown files before reading file text locally in your browser.</li>
        <li>The report checks frontmatter, `type`, recommended fields, links, and duplicate resources.</li>
        <li>Fix parsing and required-field errors before index, link, and duplicate-resource warnings.</li>
        <li>Review remaining warnings with the content owner before publishing.</li>
        <li>Run the folder check again after fixing files.</li>
      </ol>
      <CodeBlock code={sampleBundle} label="Expected bundle shape" />
    </section>

    <section class="compare-table-section">
      <h2>Single-file vs folder checks</h2>
      <div class="compare-table" role="table" aria-label="Single-file and folder validation differences">
        <div class="compare-row compare-head" role="row">
          <div role="columnheader">Check</div>
          <div role="columnheader">Use it for</div>
          <div role="columnheader">What it cannot prove</div>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-row" role="row">
          <div role="cell"><a href="/okf-validator/">OKF Validator</a></div>
          <div role="cell">One pasted Markdown file, frontmatter, required fields, and body warnings.</div>
          <div role="cell">Whether related files exist or source claims are current.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-row" role="row">
          <div role="cell">OKF Folder Validator</div>
          <div role="cell">A selected local bundle with <code>index.md</code>, duplicate resources, and relative links.</div>
          <div role="cell">Official conformance, source truth, SEO visibility, or AI citations.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Trust and privacy boundary</h2>
      <p>
        This folder validator checks this site's guide-profile structure for selected local files. It is useful before publishing, but it is not official OKF conformance, OpenAPI contract validation, or proof that the Markdown body is factually current.
      </p>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>It cannot certify official OKF conformance.</li>
        <li>It cannot prove that the facts inside the Markdown body are true or current.</li>
        <li>It cannot read files you do not select.</li>
        <li>It cannot replace CI, command-line conformance tools, security review, or source-owner approval.</li>
        <li>Use the <a href="/guides/validate-okf-bundle/">bundle validation checklist</a> and <a href="/guides/common-okf-validation-errors/">common validation errors</a> guide to fix findings before publishing.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-section">
      <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
      <h2>OKF folder validator questions</h2>
      <details>
        <summary>Does this upload my files?</summary>
        <p>No. The validation logic uses browser File APIs and prints the report in the page.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does this support ZIP upload?</summary>
        <p>Not in this MVP. Select a folder in a supported browser or select multiple Markdown files.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is a passing bundle officially certified?</summary>
        <p>No. Passing means this guide profile did not find structural errors. It is not official certification.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I use this in CI?</summary>
        <p>No. Use this page for browser review. For CI, use a local script or command-line validator.</p>
      </details>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    const folderInput = document.querySelector("#folder-input");
    const validateButton = document.querySelector("#validate-folder-button");
    const loadSampleButton = document.querySelector("#load-sample-bundle");
    const output = document.querySelector("#folder-validator-output");
    const status = document.querySelector("#folder-validator-status");
    const copyResult = document.querySelector("#copy-folder-result");
    const maxMarkdownFiles = 200;
    const maxFileSizeBytes = 1024 * 1024;
    const maxTotalBytes = 5 * 1024 * 1024;

    let sampleFiles = null;

    function formatBytes(bytes) {
      if (bytes < 1024) {
        return `${bytes} B`;
      }

      if (bytes < 1024 * 1024) {
        return `${Math.round(bytes / 1024)} KB`;
      }

      return `${(bytes / (1024 * 1024)).toFixed(1)} MB`;
    }

    function normalizePath(path) {
      return path.replaceAll("\\", "/").replace(/^\.?\//, "");
    }

    function isMarkdownPath(path) {
      return /\.(md|markdown)$/i.test(normalizePath(path));
    }

    function normalizeSegments(path) {
      const parts = [];

      normalizePath(path).split("/").forEach((part) => {
        if (!part || part === ".") {
          return;
        }

        if (part === "..") {
          parts.pop();
          return;
        }

        parts.push(part);
      });

      return parts.join("/");
    }

    function dirname(path) {
      const clean = normalizePath(path);
      const index = clean.lastIndexOf("/");
      return index === -1 ? "" : clean.slice(0, index);
    }

    function parseFrontmatter(markdown) {
      const match = markdown.match(/^---\s*\n([\s\S]*?)\n---\s*(?:\n|$)([\s\S]*)$/);

      if (!match) {
        return { frontmatter: null, body: markdown, malformedLines: [] };
      }

      const fields = {};
      const malformedLines = [];

      match[1].split(/\r?\n/).forEach((line) => {
        if (!line.trim()) {
          return;
        }

        const fieldMatch = line.match(/^([A-Za-z0-9_-]+):\s*(.*)$/);

        if (fieldMatch) {
          fields[fieldMatch[1]] = fieldMatch[2].trim();
          return;
        }

        malformedLines.push(line);
      });

      return { frontmatter: fields, body: match[2], malformedLines };
    }

    function decodeLinkPath(path) {
      try {
        return decodeURIComponent(path);
      } catch {
        return path;
      }
    }

    function resolveLink(filePath, target) {
      const trimmedTarget = target.trim();

      if (/^(https?:|mailto:|urn:|#|\/)/i.test(trimmedTarget)) {
        return null;
      }

      const withoutHash = trimmedTarget.split("#")[0];
      const withoutQuery = withoutHash.split("?")[0];
      const decodedPath = decodeLinkPath(withoutQuery);

      if (!decodedPath || !isMarkdownPath(decodedPath)) {
        return null;
      }

      return normalizeSegments(`${dirname(filePath)}/${decodedPath}`);
    }

    function validateBundle(files, preflightWarnings = []) {
      const errors = [];
      const warnings = [...preflightWarnings];
      const markdownFiles = files
        .map((file) => ({ ...file, path: normalizePath(file.path) }))
        .filter((file) => isMarkdownPath(file.path));
      const pathSet = new Set(markdownFiles.map((file) => file.path));
      const resources = new Map();

      if (markdownFiles.length === 0) {
        errors.push("No Markdown files were selected.");
      }

      if (!pathSet.has("index.md") && !Array.from(pathSet).some((path) => path.endsWith("/index.md"))) {
        warnings.push("No index.md file found. Add one to explain the bundle scope.");
      }

      markdownFiles.forEach((file) => {
        const parsed = parseFrontmatter(file.text.trim());
        const prefix = `${file.path}:`;

        if (!parsed.frontmatter) {
          errors.push(`${prefix} missing simple frontmatter block.`);
          return;
        }

        parsed.malformedLines.forEach((line) => {
          errors.push(`${prefix} invalid frontmatter line "${line}".`);
        });

        if (!parsed.frontmatter.type) {
          errors.push(`${prefix} missing required OKF field type.`);
        }

        ["title", "description", "resource", "tags", "timestamp"].forEach((field) => {
          if (!parsed.frontmatter[field]) {
            warnings.push(`${prefix} missing recommended guide field ${field}.`);
          }
        });

        if (parsed.frontmatter.tags && !/^\[.+\]$/.test(parsed.frontmatter.tags)) {
          errors.push(`${prefix} tags should use an inline array such as [okf, bundle].`);
        }

        if (parsed.frontmatter.resource) {
          const existing = resources.get(parsed.frontmatter.resource);

          if (existing) {
            warnings.push(`${prefix} resource duplicates ${existing}.`);
          } else {
            resources.set(parsed.frontmatter.resource, file.path);
          }
        }

        if (!parsed.body.trim()) {
          warnings.push(`${prefix} Markdown body is empty.`);
        }

        const relativeLinks = Array.from(parsed.body.matchAll(/\[[^\]]+\]\(([^)]+)\)/g));

        relativeLinks.forEach((match) => {
          const resolved = resolveLink(file.path, match[1]);

          if (resolved && !pathSet.has(resolved)) {
            warnings.push(`${prefix} relative link target not selected: ${match[1]}.`);
          }
        });
      });

      return {
        valid: errors.length === 0,
        checked: markdownFiles.length,
        errors,
        warnings
      };
    }

    function renderReport(result) {
      const lines = [
        `valid: ${result.valid}`,
        `markdown_files_checked: ${result.checked}`,
        "errors:",
        ...(result.errors.length ? result.errors.map((item) => `  - ${item}`) : ["  - none"]),
        "warnings:",
        ...(result.warnings.length ? result.warnings.map((item) => `  - ${item}`) : ["  - none"])
      ];

      output.textContent = lines.join("\n");
      status.textContent = result.valid ? "Valid" : "Invalid";
      status.classList.toggle("is-valid", result.valid);
      status.classList.toggle("is-invalid", !result.valid);
    }

    async function selectedFiles() {
      if (sampleFiles) {
        return { files: sampleFiles, preflightWarnings: [] };
      }

      const selected = Array.from(folderInput.files || []);
      const preflightWarnings = [];
      const markdownCandidates = selected.filter((file) => isMarkdownPath(file.webkitRelativePath || file.name));
      const skippedNonMarkdownCount = selected.length - markdownCandidates.length;
      let candidates = markdownCandidates;
      let totalBytes = 0;
      const files = [];

      if (skippedNonMarkdownCount > 0) {
        preflightWarnings.push(`${skippedNonMarkdownCount} non-Markdown file(s) skipped before reading.`);
      }

      if (candidates.length > maxMarkdownFiles) {
        preflightWarnings.push(`Only the first ${maxMarkdownFiles} Markdown file(s) were read. ${candidates.length - maxMarkdownFiles} file(s) were skipped.`);
        candidates = candidates.slice(0, maxMarkdownFiles);
      }

      for (const file of candidates) {
        const path = file.webkitRelativePath || file.name;

        if (file.size > maxFileSizeBytes) {
          preflightWarnings.push(`${path}: skipped because ${formatBytes(file.size)} exceeds the ${formatBytes(maxFileSizeBytes)} per-file limit.`);
          continue;
        }

        if (totalBytes + file.size > maxTotalBytes) {
          preflightWarnings.push(`${path}: skipped because the selected Markdown files exceed the ${formatBytes(maxTotalBytes)} total read limit.`);
          continue;
        }

        totalBytes += file.size;
        files.push({
          path,
          text: await file.text()
        });
      }

      return { files, preflightWarnings };
    }

    validateButton.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const selection = await selectedFiles();
      renderReport(validateBundle(selection.files, selection.preflightWarnings));
    });

    folderInput.addEventListener("change", () => {
      const selected = Array.from(folderInput.files || []);
      const markdownCount = selected.filter((file) => isMarkdownPath(file.webkitRelativePath || file.name)).length;

      sampleFiles = null;
      status.textContent = "Ready";
      status.classList.remove("is-valid", "is-invalid");
      output.textContent = `${selected.length} local file(s) selected; ${markdownCount} Markdown file(s) will be read. Run validation to inspect the bundle.`;
    });

    loadSampleButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
      sampleFiles = [
        {
          path: "index.md",
          text: `---
type: Knowledge Bundle
title: Website support bundle
description: Indexes reviewed website support pages.
resource: urn:okf-bundle:website-support
tags: [okf, bundle, website]
timestamp: 2026-06-21T00:00:00Z
---

# Bundle index

- [Home page](pages/home.md)
- [Contact page](support/contact.md)`
        },
        {
          path: "pages/home.md",
          text: `---
type: Website Page
title: Home page
description: Explains the site purpose and links to key tools.
resource: https://openknowledgeformat.online/
tags: [website, home, okf]
timestamp: 2026-06-21T00:00:00Z
---

# Home page

The page introduces OKF tools and links back to [the index](../index.md).`
        },
        {
          path: "support/contact.md",
          text: `---
type: Support Page
title: Contact page
description: Explains how users can report corrections.
resource: https://openknowledgeformat.online/contact/
tags: [support, contact, corrections]
timestamp: 2026-06-21T00:00:00Z
---

# Contact page

Use this file for correction routing and support boundaries.`
        }
      ];
      renderReport(validateBundle(sampleFiles));
    });

    copyResult.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const original = copyResult.textContent;

      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(output.textContent || "");
        copyResult.textContent = "Copied";
      } catch {
        copyResult.textContent = "Copy failed";
      }

      window.setTimeout(() => {
        copyResult.textContent = original;
      }, 1600);
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
